{
	title: 'Navigation preserves the current session draft',
	spec: 'Restore the invariant that session navigation never replaces an unsent draft with stale cached editor text or submit cleanup from the previous session. Terminal focus uses the latest synchronized draft even for prefetched or cached tabs, preserving caret and selection when text is unchanged and keeping recalled prompts and protected queue edits distinct. A synchronously answered navigation submit clears only its source editor, never the destination. Investigate web parity and stale empty cross-client updates with disposable fixtures; stale-revision empty updates must preserve nonempty host text. Regressions cover a hidden session updated by another client, navigation to it and continued typing, and immediate navigation during submit. Preserve local dirty draft conflict handling, optimistic sending, and lazy cached transcript loading. No live user drafts or diagnostic collection are needed.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Two terminal regressions reproduced before the fix: a hidden cached prompt stays stale while common/drafts receives current text and revision; focus restored that stale prompt. Separately, the in-process host runs slash navigation synchronously during submit, after which onKeys assigned the old cleared prompt to the newly focused destination. Subsequent typing can replace unseen text using the current revision, so host stale-revision conflict handling cannot help. Focus now reconciles editor text from shared draft/recall/queue state; onKeys stops applying source key results after the session changes. Existing setPrompt preserves caret and selection for unchanged text. Work is constant per focus, with no new persistent state or per-frame scans.',
		'Web parity: its WebSocket replies arrive after send cleanup, and tabs.show already reads current shared draft rather than cached composer text. A controller regression covers hidden cross-client updates followed by /go and typing without a navigation draft write; no web behavior change. A real-host disposable fixture confirms a stale-revision empty draft cannot erase nonempty text. Disk drafts have watch:false: external edits do not update an already-open host object. Persisted history records submitted commands, not each draft edit or client identity; a historical overwrite cannot be uniquely attributed from a revision delta alone. No live draft files were changed for this task. Public upstream tsk README supplied the tooling conventions.',
		'Validation: 104 focused terminal, browser-controller and host-draft tests pass, including four new behavioral regressions; both terminal regressions failed before the fix. Full ./test: 1462 pass, 3 fail outside the changed behavior: client/render.ts exceeds the module size limit (499 lines), host snapshot slicing expected an asynchronous snapshot, and a throwing-stream host test timed out. TypeScript and lint completed without diagnostics. No retries or timeout changes. Browser behavior was checked through controller fixtures, not a live browser; no layout or DOM code changed.'
